      "role": "user",
      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n\n## Column Mapping\n- departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- average number of enrolled students per subject: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- 2022FA term: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- departments that grant degrees: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Join Keys\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.TERM_CODE\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Electrical Engineering and Computer Science\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '6'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, give the department name and the coefficient of variation of the total units for reserved library materials, considering only terms that are regular terms and only for the Mathematics department (Course 18).\n```sql\nSELECT ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME, STDDEV(ss.TOTAL_UNITS)/NULLIF(AVG(ss.TOTAL_UNITS),0) AS coefficient_of_variation FROM LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL lrm JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON lrm.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE AND lrm.SUBJECT_ID = ss.SUBJECT_ID WHERE at.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y' AND ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME HAVING AVG(ss.TOTAL_UNITS) > 0 ORDER BY coefficient_of_variation DESC;\n```\n2. For each department, provide the department name and the range, variance, and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students per subject offered by that department in the 2022FA term, but only include departments that grant degrees and exclude the Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department (Course 6).\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_range, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_variance, STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_stddev FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE tso.TERM_CODE = '2022FA' AND sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '6' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME HAVING COUNT(tso.SUBJECT_ID) > 0 ORDER BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ;\n```\n3. List, for each department, the department name, the coefficient of variation of the total units for reserved library materials (for regular terms and only for the Mathematics department), the range, variance, and standard deviation of the number of enrolled students per subject offered by that department in the 2022FA term (only for departments that grant degrees and excluding the Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department), and the reason for inclusion ('LibraryMathematics' for the library materials statistics and 'DepartmentEnrollmentStats' for the enrollment statistics). The columns should be shown in the following order: department name, coefficient of variation, enrolled range, enrolled variance, enrolled standard deviation, and reason for inclusion.\n```sql\nWITH LibraryMathematics AS ( SELECT ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME, STDDEV(ss.TOTAL_UNITS)/NULLIF(AVG(ss.TOTAL_UNITS),0) AS coefficient_of_variation FROM LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL lrm JOIN ACADEMIC_TERMS at ON lrm.TERM_CODE = at.TERM_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON at.TERM_CODE = ss.TERM_CODE AND lrm.SUBJECT_ID = ss.SUBJECT_ID WHERE at.IS_REGULAR_TERM = 'Y' AND ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' GROUP BY ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME HAVING AVG(ss.TOTAL_UNITS) > 0 ORDER BY coefficient_of_variation DESC ), DepartmentEnrollmentStats AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) - MIN(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_range, VARIANCE(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_variance, STDDEV(tso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS enrolled_stddev FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED tso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON tso.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE tso.TERM_CODE = '2022FA' AND sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '6' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME HAVING COUNT(tso.SUBJECT_ID) > 0 ORDER BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ), CombinedDepartmentStats AS ( SELECT lm.DEPARTMENT_NAME, lm.coefficient_of_variation, NULL AS enrolled_range, NULL AS enrolled_variance, NULL AS enrolled_stddev, 'LibraryMathematics' AS Reason FROM LibraryMathematics lm UNION ALL SELECT des.DEPARTMENT_NAME, NULL AS coefficient_of_variation, des.enrolled_range, des.enrolled_variance, des.enrolled_stddev, 'DepartmentEnrollmentStats' AS Reason FROM DepartmentEnrollmentStats des ) SELECT * FROM CombinedDepartmentStats ORDER BY DEPARTMENT_NAME;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor departments where the average number of enrolled students per subject in the 2022FA term is greater than the overall average enrolled students per subject for that term (excluding the Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department and only including departments that grant degrees), list the department name and the average enrolled students per subject. Do not return any rounded answers."
